  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ There exists $y\\in R$ such that $\\frac{y}{2}$ is not real.",
  "worked_solution": "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(y):\\frac{y}{2}\\text{\u00a0is real},\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\u2203y\\in R,\\,\u00acP(y).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(\u2203y\\in R,\\,\u00acP(y)) & \u2261\u2200y\\in R,\\,\u00ac\u00acP(y) \\\\  & \u2261\u2200y\\in R,\\,P(y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $\u2200y\\in R,\\,P(y)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $y\\in R,$ $\\frac{y}{2}$ is real.",
